{"title":"Career roadmap — Writer/Editor","role":"Writer/Editor","summary":"A Writer/Editor with a Philosophy background can work across publishing, journalism, digital media, education, research, corporate communications, content strategy, technical writing, thought leadership and knowledge products.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Philosophy"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Philosophy is particularly useful for developing critical thinking, argumentation, conceptual clarity, ethics, reading comprehension and structured writing. To become employable, these abilities should be combined with professional writing, editing, digital publishing and domain expertise."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build writing, editing, research, grammar, digital publishing and portfolio skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in editorial, publishing, journalism, technical writing, corporate content or thought leadership"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress into Senior Editor, Content Strategist, Managing Editor or Editorial Lead roles"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead editorial teams, publications, content businesses, knowledge platforms or independent writing practices"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Writing foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"English grammar"},{"text":"Vocabulary"},{"text":"Sentence construction"},{"text":"Essay writing"},{"text":"Argumentative writing"},{"text":"Critical thinking"},{"text":"Reading comprehension"},{"text":"Philosophy and logic"},{"text":"Research fundamentals"},{"text":"Basic digital publishing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice different formats:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"t